## Why This Is Asked
Tests event-driven design, Cloud Run vs Cloud Functions, and idempotent outputs in GCS pipelines. It also covers IAM least privilege and basic testing strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Cloud Storage finalize events
- Cloud Functions and Cloud Run integration
- Idempotent object writes in GCS
- IAM bindings for service accounts
- Containerized image processing with ImageMagick or similar

## Code Example
```javascript
// Cloud Function (node) skeleton
exports.thumbsTrigger = async (data) => {
  const bucket = data.bucket;
  const name = data.name;
  // call Cloud Run with metadata
  await fetch(RUN_ENDPOINT, { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify({ bucket, name })});
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test locally and with CI for this flow?
- How would you handle transient failures and retries without duplicating work?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses designing scalable, tenant-isolated ingestion pipelines on GCP, focusing on Dataflow exact-once processing, per-tenant isolation, and cost controls.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant isolation and data residency
- Dataflow streaming exact-once and dedup
- Storage and BigQuery schema design
- IAM least-privilege, Private Service Connect
- Schema evolution and testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-beam snippet: deduplicate by event_id
const seen = new Set();
if (!seen.has(event.event_id)) {
  emit(event);
  seen.add(event.event_id);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test migrations to a growing tenant base?
- How would you enforce per-tenant quotas and SLAs?

